# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
!coverage.go
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env
*.env

# AgentSpillCheck local data and session artefacts (PLAN 17.1)
.spillcheck/
test/tmp/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
report*.html
!docs/report-samples/report*.html
/dist/
/spillcheck

# Product spec, ADR log and progress tracking are local-only (owner decision).
# Keep working copies locally; never push them.
docs/PROGRESS.md
docs/PLAN.md
docs/decisions/

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Video demo project: track render sources (src, package.json,
# package-lock.json, tsconfig.json, vo/*.txt narration scripts) plus
# the final EN demo mp4 for GitHub preview. Everything regenerable
# or installable stays local: deps, intermediate out/ files,
# copied public/ render inputs, and generated voiceover audio.
video/node_modules/
video/out/*
!video/out/agent-spillcheck-demo.mp4
!video/out/demo-poster.jpg
video/public/
video/vo/*.aiff
video/vo/*.wav
